sections.text:
Common mistakes include mixing units, especially between SI and older mixed units. Another is using a formula outside its assumptions, such as using incompressible aerodynamics at high Mach number.

Other errors are:
forgetting body forces or pressure forces in a control-volume analysis;
confusing mass flow with volume flow;
using the wrong reference area or chord in lift and moment coefficients;
sign errors in stability and control derivatives;
ignoring units in software input and accepting output because it looks precise;
copying a design rule without checking the country, aircraft category and current revision.

State your assumptions and show the steps. An examiner, like a senior engineer, needs to see how you reached the answer.
